-- title:
--   Order of the toric m-torsion subgroup: m^{toricRank}
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ and $p$ be natural numbers with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and suppose $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure of $\mathbf{Q}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that the image of $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a level datum of level $N_0$ at $p$ over $A$, that is, a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\mathrm{base}\,p$, a relative group law on $f$ over $\mathrm{baseRing}\,p$, and bijections from $\mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ and from $\mathrm{JZeroC}$ over the residue field of $A$ onto the sections of $f$ over the generic and the residual point respectively; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies the predicate `IsJacobian`, the conjunction of the abelian-scheme property bundle for $\Lambda.f$, commutativity of the group law, additivity and Galois-equivariance of the two point parametrisations, compatibility of reduction of points modulo $\Lambda$'s data, and realisability of every element of the Hecke algebra by an endomorphism of $f$ respecting the group law. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a Néron object at $p$ of level $N_0p$ over this datum, namely a scheme $G$ over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ carrying a commutative relative group law whose structure morphism is smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact and surjective with preconnected fibres, together with an additive, Galois-equivariant and Hecke-compatible bijection from $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ onto the sections over the generic point, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by every $n > 0$, properness of the generic fibre, a natural number $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricRank}$, and further data including the family $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPoint}$. Then for every $m > 0$ the subgroup $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ generated by the range of $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ is finite of cardinality exactly $m^{\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricRank}}$.
--
--   This computes the order of the group generated by the $m$-torsion of the toric part of the Néron object at $p$ in level $N_0p$: it is $m^{t}$ with $t$ the toric rank, as for $\mu_m^t$ in characteristic zero. It supplies the cardinality field used when assembling the numerical data attached to the Néron object, and is cited in the construction of those data and in the characterisation of membership in $\mathcal{O}.\mathrm{toricPts}$ via the fibre maps.
